    "['ptp clock domain [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ptp clock-mode boundary domain 1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols ptp clock-mode boundary domain 1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration command for `ptp clock domain 1`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols ptp clock-mode boundary domain 1\\n##\\n\\nOr alternatively, if you need a more basic PTP domain configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols ptp domain 1\\n##\\n\\nThe first option is more precise as it also specifies the boundary clock mode (equivalent to Cisco's `ptp device-type bc` in the original config). The second option just sets the domain if that's the only requirement.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols ptp clock-mode boundary domain 1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ptp domain 1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols ptp domain 1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration command for `ptp clock domain 1`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols ptp clock-mode boundary domain 1\\n##\\n\\nOr alternatively, if you need a more basic PTP domain configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols ptp domain 1\\n##\\n\\nThe first option is more precise as it also specifies the boundary clock mode (equivalent to Cisco's `ptp device-type bc` in the original config). The second option just sets the domain if that's the only requirement.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols ptp domain 1'}]]": 1,
