    "['no shutdown', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, `no shutdown` (Cisco) translates to enabling the interface by default (since interfaces are enabled by default in Juniper). To explicitly disable an interface in Juniper, you\\'d use `set interfaces <name> disable`. However, if the intent is to keep the interface enabled (as `no shutdown` does in Cisco), no equivalent command is needed in Juniper (as it\\'s the default state). \\n\\nIf you specifically want the \"enable\" equivalent in Juniper, you\\'d use:\\n##\\ndelete interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable\\n##\\nBut this is only necessary if the interface was previously disabled. \\n\\nThe most accurate translation of `no shutdown` (enable the interface) in Juniper is to ensure no `disable` statement exists, hence the `delete` form above.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'delete interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, `no shutdown` (Cisco) translates to enabling the interface by default (since interfaces are enabled by default in Juniper). To explicitly disable an interface in Juniper, you\\'d use `set interfaces <name> disable`. However, if the intent is to keep the interface enabled (as `no shutdown` does in Cisco), no equivalent command is needed in Juniper (as it\\'s the default state). \\n\\nIf you specifically want the \"enable\" equivalent in Juniper, you\\'d use:\\n##\\ndelete interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable\\n##\\nBut this is only necessary if the interface was previously disabled. \\n\\nThe most accurate translation of `no shutdown` (enable the interface) in Juniper is to ensure no `disable` statement exists, hence the `delete` form above.', 'trans_template': 'delete interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable'}]]": 1,
